Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:51:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 17/71] Offer the reasoning levels GLM-5.3 actually accepts

The catalog advertised `none`, `low`, `medium` and `high`, a ladder copied
from a model that is not the one being shipped. GLM-5.3 and GLM-5.3-Flash
take `low`, `high` and `max` and error on everything else, so two of the four
entries in the picker could not be honoured and the rung a user would reach
for on a hard problem was missing.

The default moves to `high`, which Z.ai measures as holding most of `max`'s
score for about a third fewer output tokens. `max` is reachable but not by
accident: the TUI treats it as an advanced effort, so the Alt+, and Alt+.
shortcuts step between low and high and the deepest rung is an explicit trip
through the model picker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 codex-rs/models-manager/models.json | 14 +++++---------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json b/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json
index fc74951acd..40c36bff0c 100644
--- a/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json
+++ b/codex-rs/models-manager/models.json
@@ -33,23 +33,19 @@
       "default_reasoning_summary": "none",
       "display_name": "GLM 5.3",
       "description": "Fast agentic coding model.",
-      "default_reasoning_level": "medium",
+      "default_reasoning_level": "high",
       "supported_reasoning_levels": [
-        {
-          "effort": "none",
-          "description": "No extended thinking; fastest and cheapest"
-        },
         {
           "effort": "low",
           "description": "Fast responses with lighter reasoning"
         },
-        {
-          "effort": "medium",
-          "description": "Balances speed and reasoning depth for everyday tasks"
-        },
         {
           "effort": "high",
           "description": "Greater reasoning depth for complex problems"
+        },
+        {
+          "effort": "max",
+          "description": "Deepest reasoning; slowest and most expensive"
         }
       ],
       "shell_type": "unified_exec",
